 "notes": "Own WBADB row has no pool, pit or grave. SWP: Mem III p. 220 Tell es Sultan entry used (spring reservoir on the east; Warren's graves in mound No. 3 'south of 'Ain es Sultan', coded relative_to other = the spring). Warren's own excavation shafts (1868) not coded. Other SWP entries describe different places with no stated distance or direction from the unit and none shown within 2 km; ignored: Kusr el Yehud (cistern), Rujm el Mogheifir (cisterns), Beit Jubr et Tahtani (birkeh; matched on 'Birket es Sultan at Jerusalem'), Kanat Musa (aqueduct cisterns, Birket Musa, Bir Heider), Hajr el Asbah, Kh. es Sumrah (caves), Kanat el Manil (well), Kh. el Mefjir (no pool/pit/grave). Nigro N85 is the tell itself (2 m, bearing invalid); its features take grid N85. N21 'pool' listed under Ottoman coded L; 'roofed pool' (Modern) coded as pit per PROTOCOL 3; Roman 'nympheum' coded pool_def unclear. N47 has no coordinates: coded words SW relative_to other (site n. 46). Natural niches, recesses, fissures, rock shelters and the 'not examined' rows were not coded; caves, cavities and passages coded as pits. Avi'or Cave '38 skeletons' and 'human bones' in other caves not coded as graves (not called burials); Cave of the Sandal '17 ... burials' coded as a grave in addition to the cave."
